{"id":"mahabharata-3-197","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":197,"title":"सप्तनवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 197 · Kaushika and the devoted wife","summary":{"en":"The Brahmin Kaushika burns a crane to death with an angry look, then goes begging and is kept waiting by a housewife who first serves her returning husband. When he rebukes her, she tells him she is no crane, reveals that she knows what happened in the forest, and sends him to learn dharma from a meat-seller in Mithila.","kn":"ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ಕೌಶಿಕನು ಕೋಪದ ನೋಟದಿಂದ ಬಕವನ್ನು ಸುಟ್ಟು, ಭಿಕ್ಷೆಗೆ ಹೋದಾಗ ಮರಳಿದ ಪತಿಯ ಸೇವೆ ಮೊದಲು ಮಾಡಿದ ಗೃಹಿಣಿಯಿಂದ ಕಾಯಿಸಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನು ಆಕ್ಷೇಪಿಸಿದಾಗ ತಾನು ಬಕವಲ್ಲ ಎಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆದದ್ದನ್ನು ತಿಳಿದಿರುವುದನ್ನು ತೋರಿಸಿ, ಧರ್ಮ ಕಲಿಯಲು ಮಿಥಿಲೆಯ ಮಾಂಸ ಮಾರುವವನ ಬಳಿಗೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"ब्राह्मण कौशिक क्रोध भरी दृष्टि से एक बगुले को जला देते हैं, फिर भिक्षा माँगने जाते हैं और एक गृहिणी उन्हें प्रतीक्षा कराती है क्योंकि वह पहले लौटे पति की सेवा करती है। जब वे उसे फटकारते हैं, वह कहती है कि वह बगुला नहीं है, वन की घटना जानने की बात प्रकट करती है, और उन्हें मिथिला के एक मांस-विक्रेता से धर्म सीखने भेजती है।","te":"బ్రాహ్మణుడు కౌశికుడు కోపపు చూపుతో కొంగను కాల్చివేసి, భిక్షకు వెళ్లగా తిరిగివచ్చిన భర్తకు ముందుగా సేవ చేసిన గృహిణి అతనిని వేచి ఉంచుతుంది. అతడు ఆక్షేపించగా తాను కొంగను కానని చెప్పి అడవిలో జరిగినది తనకు తెలుసని వెల్లడించి, ధర్మం నేర్చుకోవడానికి మిథిలలోని మాంసవిక్రేత వద్దకు పంపుతుంది.","ta":"அந்தணர் கௌஶிகர் சினப் பார்வையால் ஒரு கொக்கை எரித்துவிட்டுப் பிச்சைக்குச் செல்ல, திரும்பி வந்த கணவனுக்கு முதலில் பணிவிடை செய்த இல்லத்தரசி அவரைக் காக்க வைக்கிறாள். அவர் கடிய, தான் கொக்கு அல்ல என்று சொல்லிக் காட்டில் நடந்ததைத் தான் அறிவதை வெளிப்படுத்தி, அறம் கற்க மிதிலையிலுள்ள ஓர் இறைச்சி வணிகரிடம் அனுப்புகிறாள்.","ml":"കൗശികൻ എന്ന ബ്രാഹ്മണൻ കോപദൃഷ്ടികൊണ്ട് ഒരു കൊക്കിനെ ചുട്ടുകൊല്ലുന്നു; പിന്നെ ഭിക്ഷയ്ക്ക് പോയപ്പോൾ, മടങ്ങിയെത്തിയ ഭർത്താവിനെ ആദ്യം പരിചരിക്കുന്ന ഒരു വീട്ടമ്മ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ കാത്തിരുത്തുന്നു. അദ്ദേഹം ശാസിച്ചപ്പോൾ, താൻ കൊക്കല്ലെന്നും കാട്ടിൽ നടന്നത് തനിക്കറിയാമെന്നും അവൾ പറയുന്നു; മിഥിലയിലെ ഒരു മാംസവ്യാപാരിയിൽനിന്ന് ധർമ്മം പഠിക്കാൻ അവനെ അയക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.197; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कश्चिद्द्विजातिप्रवरो वेदाध्यायी तपोधनः ।\nतपस्वी धर्मशीलश्च कौशिको नाम भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was a certain foremost brahmin, a student of the Veda, rich in austerity, an ascetic of righteous habits, named Kaushika, Bharata."}},{"n":2,"text":"साङ्गोपनिषदान्वेदानधीते द्विजसत्तमः ।\nस वृक्षमूले कस्मिंश्चिद्वेदानुच्चारयन्स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of brahmins studied the Vedas with their limbs and the Upanishads. Once he stood at the foot of a tree, reciting the Vedas."}},{"n":3,"text":"उपरिष्टाच्च वृक्षस्य बलाका संन्यलीयत ।\nतया पुरीषमुत्सृष्टं ब्राह्मणस्य तदोपरि ॥","meaning":{"en":"A crane perched on top of the tree, and it dropped its dung on the brahmin."}},{"n":4,"text":"तामवेक्ष्य ततः क्रुद्धः समपध्यायत द्विजः ।\nभृशं क्रोधाभिभूतेन बलाका सा निरीक्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing it, the brahmin grew angry and wished it harm, and the crane was looked at by him in extreme anger."}},{"n":5,"text":"अपध्याता च विप्रेण न्यपतद्वसुधातले ।\nबलाकां पतितां दृष्ट्वा गतसत्त्वामचेतनाम् ।\nकारुण्यादभिसंतप्तः पर्यशोचत तां द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cursed by the brahmin, the crane fell to the ground. Seeing the crane fallen, lifeless and unconscious, the brahmin was pained with compassion and grieved for it."}},{"n":6,"text":"अकार्यं कृतवानस्मि रागद्वेषबलात्कृतः ।\nइत्युक्त्वा बहुशो विद्वान्ग्रामं भैक्षाय संश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have done what I should not, driven by passion and aversion,\" the learned man said many times; then he went to a village to beg."}},{"n":7,"text":"ग्रामे शुचीनि प्रचरन्कुलानि भरतर्षभ ।\nप्रविष्टस्तत्कुलं यत्र पूर्वं चरितवांस्तु सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going through the village to pure households, best of the Bharatas, he entered a house which he had visited before."}},{"n":8,"text":"देहीति याचमानो वै तिष्ठेत्युक्तः स्त्रिया ततः ।\nशौचं तु यावत्कुरुते भाजनस्य कुटुम्बिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"He asked, \"Give me alms,\" but the woman of the house said, \"Wait,\" while she was cleaning the vessel."}},{"n":9,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे राजन्क्षुधासंपीडितो भृशम् ।\nभर्ता प्रविष्टः सहसा तस्या भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the meantime, king, her husband, greatly pressed by hunger, suddenly came in, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":10,"text":"सा तु दृष्ट्वा पतिं साध्वी ब्राह्मणं व्यपहाय तम् ।\nपाद्यमाचमनीयं च ददौ भर्त्रे तथासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the good woman, seeing her husband, left that brahmin and gave her husband water for his feet, water for rinsing his mouth and a seat."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रह्वा पर्यचरच्चापि भर्तारमसितेक्षणा ।\nआहारेणाथ भक्ष्यैश्च वाक्यैः सुमधुरैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dark-eyed wife, bowing, waited on her husband with food, snacks and very sweet words."}},{"n":12,"text":"उच्छिष्टं भुञ्जते भर्तुः सा तु नित्यं युधिष्ठिर ।\nदैवतं च पतिं मेने भर्तुश्चित्तानुसारिणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"She always ate her husband's leftovers, Yudhishthira, regarded her husband as a god, and followed her husband's mind."}},{"n":13,"text":"न कर्मणा न मनसा नात्यश्नान्नापि चापिबत् ।\nतं सर्वभावोपगता पतिशुश्रूषणे रता ॥","meaning":{"en":"She did not eat or drink excessively, in deed or in thought; devoted in every way to serving her husband."}},{"n":14,"text":"साध्वाचारा शुचिर्दक्षा कुटुम्बस्य हितैषिणी ।\nभर्तुश्चापि हितं यत्तत्सततं सानुवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of good conduct, pure and capable, wishing well to the family, she always followed whatever was good for her husband."}},{"n":15,"text":"देवतातिथिभृत्यानां श्वश्रूश्वशुरयोस्तथा ।\nशुश्रूषणपरा नित्यं सततं संयतेन्द्रिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was always devoted to serving the gods, guests, servants, and her mother-in-law and father-in-law, always with controlled senses."}},{"n":16,"text":"सा ब्राह्मणं तदा दृष्ट्वा संस्थितं भैक्षकाङ्क्षिणम् ।\nकुर्वती पतिशुश्रूषां सस्माराथ शुभेक्षणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, while serving her husband, that fair-eyed woman saw the brahmin standing waiting for alms and remembered him."}},{"n":17,"text":"व्रीडिता साभवत्साध्वी तदा भरतसत्तम ।\nभिक्षामादाय विप्राय निर्जगाम यशस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The good woman, best of the Bharatas, was ashamed then; the renowned lady took alms and came out to the brahmin."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"किमिदं भवति त्वं मां तिष्ठेत्युक्त्वा वराङ्गने ।\nउपरोधं कृतवती न विसर्जितवत्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is this, fair lady? Having told me to wait, you have kept me held up and not sent me off."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"ब्राह्मणं क्रोधसंतप्तं ज्वलन्तमिव तेजसा ।\nदृष्ट्वा साध्वी मनुष्येन्द्र सान्त्वपूर्वं वचोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the brahmin burning with anger and seeming to blaze with his radiance, king, the good woman spoke in a soothing way."}},{"n":20,"text":"क्षन्तुमर्हसि मे विप्र भर्ता मे दैवतं महत् ।\nस चापि क्षुधितः श्रान्तः प्राप्तः शुश्रूषितो मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should forgive me, brahmin; my husband is my great god. He was hungry and tired when he came, and I was attending him."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"ब्राह्मणा न गरीयांसो गरीयांस्ते पतिः कृतः ।\nगृहस्थधर्मे वर्तन्ती ब्राह्मणानवमन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins are not weightier; you have made your husband weightier. Living as a householder, you disrespect brahmins."}},{"n":22,"text":"इन्द्रोऽप्येषां प्रणमते किं पुनर्मानुषा भुवि ।\nअवलिप्ते न जानीषे वृद्धानां न श्रुतं त्वया ।\nब्राह्मणा ह्यग्निसदृशा दहेयुः पृथिवीमपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even Indra bows to them, what of humans on earth? Proud woman, you do not know; you have not heard from the elders that brahmins are like fire and could burn even the earth."}},{"text":"स्त्र्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"The woman said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"नावजानाम्यहं विप्रान्देवैस्तुल्यान्मनस्विनः ।\nअपराधमिमं विप्र क्षन्तुमर्हसि मेऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not disrespect brahmins, who are high-minded and equal to gods. You should forgive me this offence, blameless brahmin."}},{"n":24,"text":"जानामि तेजो विप्राणां महाभाग्यं च धीमताम् ।\nअपेयः सागरः क्रोधात्कृतो हि लवणोदकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know the power and great fortune of wise brahmins: the sea became salty and undrinkable through their anger."}},{"n":25,"text":"तथैव दीप्ततपसां मुनीनां भावितात्मनाम् ।\nयेषां क्रोधाग्निरद्यापि दण्डके नोपशाम्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too of the sages of blazing austerity and perfected souls, whose fire of anger in the Dandaka forest does not die even today."}},{"n":26,"text":"ब्राह्मणानां परिभवाद्वातापिश्च दुरात्मवान् ।\nअगस्त्यमृषिमासाद्य जीर्णः क्रूरो महासुरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through disrespect for brahmins the wicked great demon Vatapi, cruel, was digested after coming to the seer Agastya."}},{"n":27,"text":"प्रभावा बहवश्चापि श्रूयन्ते ब्रह्मवादिनाम् ।\nक्रोधः सुविपुलो ब्रह्मन्प्रसादश्च महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many powers of the speakers of Brahman are heard of, brahmin; great is the anger, and also the grace, of the great-souled."}},{"n":28,"text":"अस्मिंस्त्वतिक्रमे ब्रह्मन्क्षन्तुमर्हसि मेऽनघ ।\nपतिशुश्रूषया धर्मो यः स मे रोचते द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this transgression, brahmin, you should forgive me, blameless one. The dharma of serving my husband is what I love, brahmin."}},{"n":29,"text":"दैवतेष्वपि सर्वेषु भर्ता मे दैवतं परम् ।\nअविशेषेण तस्याहं कुर्यां धर्मं द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among all the gods my husband is my highest god. I do his duty without exception, best of brahmins."}},{"n":30,"text":"शुश्रूषायाः फलं पश्य पत्युर्ब्राह्मण यादृशम् ।\nबलाका हि त्वया दग्धा रोषात्तद्विदितं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"See what the fruit of serving the husband is like: you burned the crane in anger, and I know that."}},{"n":31,"text":"क्रोधः शत्रुः शरीरस्थो मनुष्याणां द्विजोत्तम ।\nयः क्रोधमोहौ त्यजति तं देवा ब्राह्मणं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anger, best of brahmins, is an enemy lodged in the body of men. The gods call a brahmin the one who gives up anger and delusion."}},{"n":32,"text":"यो वदेदिह सत्यानि गुरुं संतोषयेत च ।\nहिंसितश्च न हिंसेत तं देवा ब्राह्मणं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods call a brahmin the one who speaks truth here, pleases his teacher and, when harmed, does not harm back."}},{"n":33,"text":"जितेन्द्रियो धर्मपरः स्वाध्यायनिरतः शुचिः ।\nकामक्रोधौ वशे यस्य तं देवा ब्राह्मणं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods call a brahmin the one who has conquered the senses, is devoted to dharma, intent on Vedic study and pure, with desire and anger under control."}},{"n":34,"text":"यस्य चात्मसमो लोको धर्मज्ञस्य मनस्विनः ।\nसर्वधर्मेषु च रतस्तं देवा ब्राह्मणं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods call a brahmin the one who treats the world as himself, who knows dharma, is thoughtful and delights in all duties."}},{"n":35,"text":"योऽध्यापयेदधीयीत यजेद्वा याजयीत वा ।\nदद्याद्वापि यथाशक्ति तं देवा ब्राह्मणं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods call a brahmin the one who teaches or studies, sacrifices or performs sacrifice for others, and gives according to his ability."}},{"n":36,"text":"ब्रह्मचारी च वेदान्यो अधीयीत द्विजोत्तमः ।\nस्वाध्याये चाप्रमत्तो वै तं देवा ब्राह्मणं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods call a brahmin the best of the twice-born who lives as a celibate student, studies the Vedas and is not careless in study."}},{"n":37,"text":"यद्ब्राह्मणानां कुशलं तदेषां परिकीर्तयेत् ।\nसत्यं तथा व्याहरतां नानृते रमते मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should declare what is good for brahmins, and a mind speaking truth does not delight in falsehood."}},{"n":38,"text":"धनं तु ब्राह्मणस्याहुः स्वाध्यायं दममार्जवम् ।\nइन्द्रियाणां निग्रहं च शाश्वतं द्विजसत्तम ।\nसत्यार्जवे धर्ममाहुः परं धर्मविदो जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say a brahmin's wealth is study, self-restraint, honesty and control of the senses, lasting, best of brahmins; those who know dharma say truth and honesty are the highest dharma."}},{"n":39,"text":"दुर्ज्ञेयः शाश्वतो धर्मः स तु सत्ये प्रतिष्ठितः ।\nश्रुतिप्रमाणो धर्मः स्यादिति वृद्धानुशासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eternal dharma is hard to know, but it rests on truth; the elders' teaching is that dharma has the Veda as its authority."}},{"n":40,"text":"बहुधा दृश्यते धर्मः सूक्ष्म एव द्विजोत्तम ।\nभवानपि च धर्मज्ञः स्वाध्यायनिरतः शुचिः ।\nन तु तत्त्वेन भगवन्धर्मान्वेत्सीति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma is seen in many ways and is subtle, best of brahmins. You also know dharma, devoted to study and pure; but I think, revered one, that you do not know dharma truly."}},{"n":41,"text":"मातापितृभ्यां शुश्रूषुः सत्यवादी जितेन्द्रियः ।\nमिथिलायां वसन्व्याधः स ते धर्मान्प्रवक्ष्यति ।\nतत्र गच्छस्व भद्रं ते यथाकामं द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a hunter living in Mithila who serves his mother and father, speaks truth and has controlled his senses; he will tell you dharma. Go there, may it be well with you, best of brahmins, as you wish."}},{"n":42,"text":"अत्युक्तमपि मे सर्वं क्षन्तुमर्हस्यनिन्दित ।\nस्त्रियो ह्यवध्याः सर्वेषां ये धर्मविदुषो जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Forgive me everything even if I have said too much, blameless one; for women are not to be harmed by any who know dharma."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"प्रीतोऽस्मि तव भद्रं ते गतः क्रोधश्च शोभने ।\nउपालम्भस्त्वया ह्युक्तो मम निःश्रेयसं परम् ।\nस्वस्ति तेऽस्तु गमिष्यामि साधयिष्यामि शोभने ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am pleased with you, may you be well; my anger is gone, lovely one. The reproach you gave is the highest good for me. Blessings on you; I will go and accomplish it, lovely lady."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":44,"text":"तया विसृष्टो निर्गम्य स्वमेव भवनं ययौ ।\nविनिन्दन्स द्विजोऽऽत्मानं कौशिको नरसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dismissed by her, he left and went to his own house, reproaching himself, that brahmin Kaushika, best of men."}}]}]}